\section{Unstructured Dynamic Tetrahedral Complex (UDTC)}

Let \(\mathcal{T}\) be a tetrahedral complex
\[
\mathcal{T} = \{ T_i \mid i \in \mathbb{N} \},
\]
where each tetrahedron \(T_i\) has vertices
\[
T_i = (V_{i0}, V_{i1}, V_{i2}, V_{i3}), \quad V_{ij} \in \mathbb{R}^3.
\]

We attach physical fields to each tetrahedron:
\[
\rho_i = \rho(T_i), \quad
\chi_i = \chi(T_i), \quad
g_{\mu\nu}^{(i)} = g_{\mu\nu}(T_i).
\]

The memory layout is Structure-of-Arrays (SoA):
\[
\{\rho_i\}_{i=1}^N, \quad
\{\chi_i\}_{i=1}^N, \quad
\{g_{\mu\nu}^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^N.
\]